1\cdot a - 1\cdot 1 + 2\cdot c &= 0,\\
2\cdot a + 4\cdot 1 + 1\cdot c &= 0.
\end{align*}
Solving this system of equations yields
\begin{align*}
2a + c + 4 &= 0,\\
a + 2c - 1 &= 0.
\end{align*}
We add twice the equation in the $+c$ position to the equation in the $+a$ position to obtain $5a+4=0$. From this we get $a=4/5,$ in which case the solution is $a=4/5$ and $c=-14/5$. Thus, the answer is $(4/5, -14/5).$
