Let \[\lfloor x\rfloor =a\] Then
\begin{align}
a-19\left \lfloor \frac{a}{19} \right \rfloor&=9 , \\
a-89\left \lfloor \frac{a}{89} \right \rfloor&=9.
\end{align}
Notice that $a=9$ works, so let's try to generalize all the way to $\mathbb{Z}^{+}$
\begin{align}
a-19\left \lfloor \frac{a}{19} \right \rfloor&=9 , \\
a-89\left \lfloor \frac{a}{89} \right \rfloor&=9.
\end{align}
Now by Euler's Theorem This holds if 
\begin{align}
a&=9+k\phi(19)=9+18k , \\
a&=9+k\phi(89)=9+88k , 
\end{align}
if $k=N-s$ we have
\begin{align}
a&=9+(18N-18s) , \\
a&=9+(88N-88s) , 
\end{align}
Now notice that both expressions give negative values for s, but since we know that $18s=88s$ we see that adding $s=23k$ to the equations will take care of that. So let's see that the calculations hold for $23k$.
$$a=18+18k ,$$ $$a=88+88k$$ 
which is $100000000000000000+1$.

